  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "YsfH0CtqNiGLHfnAcoeOn5s/e60=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:03.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Which revision the timeline is parked on is not editor-local state. It lives in the same global store the rest of `reactor-browser`'s selection state uses, so an editor, a drive app and Connect's own chrome all observe the same value.\n\nTwo getter/setter pairs:\n\n```ts\nfunction useSelectedTimelineItem(): TimelineItem | null | undefined;\nfunction setSelectedTimelineItem(item: TimelineItem | null | undefined): void;\n\nfunction useSelectedTimelineRevision(): string | number | null | undefined;\nfunction setSelectedTimelineRevision(rev: string | number | null | undefined): void;\n```\n\nThe setters are plain functions, not hooks \u2014 call them from an event handler without violating the rules of hooks.\n\n`TimelineItem` is a union of two shapes. `TimelineBarItem` (`type: \"bar\"`) is a change candle: `revision`, `timestampUtcMs`, `startDate`/`endDate`, raw `additions`/`deletions` counts, and the bucketed `addSize`/`delSize` fields typed as `0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4`. That bucketing is worth noticing \u2014 the render height is a five-step scale, not a raw count, so the bar is comparable across documents of wildly different churn. `TimelineDividerItem` (`type: \"divider\"`) is a labelled separator instead: `title`, `subtitle`, plus the same `revision`, `timestampUtcMs` and date fields.\n\nEvery field except `id` and `type` is optional on both variants, so a consumer reading `item.revision` must handle `undefined`.\n\nNote the two values are tracked separately: the *item* and the *revision* are distinct pieces of state, and `useSelectedTimelineRevision` accepts a `string | number`, so it can hold a revision identifier the timeline never produced a bar for. Reading revision directly is the cheaper path when all you need is \"which point in history am I rendering\".\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/05-EditorsUI/01-ReactHooks.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:36:03.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:03.000Z"
    }
  },
